---
// The band that says every generated pipeline has run before you get it.
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<aside class="tg-validated not-content">
	<p class="claim">Every pipeline terragucci generates has already run.</p>
	<p>
		Each one runs against an AWS emulator before it ships: on a Forgejo or GitLab server with its runner,
		and on GitHub under act against a mock API. Each property is checked twice. Once it must hold, and once, deliberately broken, it must fail.
	</p>
	<a href={`${base}/reference/validation/`}>How validation works</a>
</aside>

<style>
	.tg-validated {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--tg-rule);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--tg-rule);
		padding: 2rem 0;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.75rem;
	}
	.claim {
		margin: 0;
		font-family: var(--tg-display);
		font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
		text-wrap: balance;
	}
	p {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 60ch;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	a {
		color: var(--sl-color-accent-high);
		font-weight: 600;
	}
</style>
